IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa10-types`
IMPORT `coa10-period`

-- coa10-filing.l4: Chapter 10, ss 441 and 443A to 447 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom): the directors' duty to
-- deliver accounts and reports to the registrar, and what each description of company must (or may) deliver.
-- Lines 5897-5907 and 5936-6059 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the rule.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words ("does not apply", "must not", "unless", "if" not met, a "where" not
--               met). Each such branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the words>"`.
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide it: silent, a list not closed, points outside the text, or limited by its own
--               wording. Each such branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The three-valued helpers `s 441 both ...`, `s 441 either ...` and `s 441 the opposite of ...` combine MAYBE BOOLEAN seam
-- answers by Kleene's rules: a JUST FALSE they return comes from an input's own JUST FALSE (the answering section's no).
--
-- TWO TEXTS. The file prints two texts of s 444, of s 445(7) and of s 446(5) (see coa10-types.l4). Where a rule depends
-- on the text, the caller states which text it relies on, as a `s 441 text of the sections the file prints twice`.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers: three-valued AND, OR and NOT over MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 441 both are true` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (x AND y)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN IF x THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN IF y THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 441 either is true` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (x OR y)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN IF x THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN IF y THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 441 the opposite of` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (NOT x)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The facts the filing sections read about a company, and about what is delivered
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Each classification is another part's answer, taken as an INPUT of type MAYBE BOOLEAN (PLAN.md section 4): a NOTHING
-- from the answering section stays NOTHING here.
DECLARE `s 441 facts about the company` HAS
    `s 441 the text of the sections the file prints twice that the caller relies on` IS A `s 441 text of the sections the file prints twice`
    `s 384A the company qualifies as a micro-entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 384B the company would qualify as a micro-entity but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 381 the company is subject to the small companies regime` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 384 the company would be subject to the small companies regime but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 415A the company is entitled to small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 465 the company qualifies as medium-sized` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 385(3) the company is an unquoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 385(2) the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- The facts of a delivery that the tables below read. "exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that
-- exemption" is Part 16's (ss 475 to 479A), a seam of this part (NOTES.md, Seams).
DECLARE `s 441 facts about what is delivered` HAS
    `s 475(1) the company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 441 the directors deliver a copy of the profit and loss account` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 441 the balance sheet or profit and loss account is abridged under paragraph 1A of Schedule 1 to the Small Companies and Groups (Accounts and Directors' Report) Regulations 2008` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 441 there is a separate corporate governance statement` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Which section applies: the description each section opens with, and what each excludes
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A description is met, not met, or not known; the seam answers are three-valued. For a company the description does
-- not fit, the section's own answer is NOTHING ("limited by its own wording"), never JUST FALSE.

-- src:5938 | (1) The directors of a company that qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to a financial year, or that would do so but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group—
@ref s 443A(1) Filing obligations of micro-entities: the description (src:5938)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 443A(1) the company is described by section 443A` MEANS
    `s 441 either is true`
        (facts's `s 384A the company qualifies as a micro-entity`)
        (facts's `s 384B the company would qualify as a micro-entity but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group`)

-- The first text of s 444 describes "a company subject to the small companies regime"; the second adds "or that would be
-- so subject but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group".
-- src:5949 | (1) The directors of a company subject to the small companies regime—
-- src:5983 | (1) The directors of a company that is subject to the small companies regime in relation to a financial year, or that would be so subject but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group, must deliver to the registrar a copy of—
@ref s 444(1) Filing obligations of companies subject to the small companies regime: the description (src:5949 and src:5983)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444(1) the company is described by section 444` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `s 441 the text of the sections the file prints twice that the caller relies on`
    WHEN `s 441 first text in the file` THEN facts's `s 381 the company is subject to the small companies regime`
    WHEN `s 441 second text in the file` THEN
        `s 441 either is true`
            (facts's `s 381 the company is subject to the small companies regime`)
            (facts's `s 384 the company would be subject to the small companies regime but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group`)

-- src:5995 | (1) The directors of a company that is entitled to small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report for a financial year—
@ref s 444A(1) Filing obligations of companies entitled to small companies exemption in relation to directors' report: the description (src:5995)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444A(1) the company is described by section 444A` MEANS
    facts's `s 415A the company is entitled to small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report`

-- src:6006 | (1)) The directors of a company that qualifies as a medium-sized company in relation to a financial year (see sections 465 to 467) must deliver to the registrar a copy of—
@ref s 445(1) Filing obligations of medium-sized companies: the description (src:6006)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445(1) the company is described by section 445` MEANS
    facts's `s 465 the company qualifies as medium-sized`

-- src:6026 | (1) The directors of an unquoted company must deliver to the registrar for each financial year of the company a copy of—
@ref s 446(1) Filing obligations of unquoted companies: the description (src:6026)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 446(1) the company is described by section 446` MEANS
    facts's `s 385(3) the company is an unquoted company`

-- src:6048 | (1) The directors of a quoted company must deliver to the registrar for each financial year of the company a copy of—
@ref s 447(1) Filing obligations of quoted companies: the description (src:6048)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 447(1) the company is described by section 447` MEANS
    facts's `s 385(2) the company is a quoted company`

-- A section applies when the company fits its description and is not within a section it excludes. Each section's own
-- "does not apply to companies within ..." sentence is a flat negative: when the company is within an excluded section the
-- answer is JUST FALSE whatever the description; a company the description does not fit gets NOTHING.
GIVEN `the company fits the description` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is within a section the text excludes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 441(1) a filing section applies given its description and its exclusions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the company is within a section the text excludes`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to companies within ..." (s 444(6) in the second text, s 444A(5), s 445(7), s 446(5))
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        CONSIDER `the company fits the description`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the company is not one the section describes
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answering section for the description gave no answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the company fits the description`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the company is not one the section describes
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is within an excluded section is not known
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answering sections gave no answer

-- ---- which sections an excluded company is within (the "does not apply to companies within ..." sentences) ----
-- INTERNAL: `within` answers JUST TRUE (the company is within the section), JUST FALSE (it is not) or NOTHING (not known).
-- The section's own answer to a person is `... section N applies to the company` below.

-- src:5938 | (1) The directors of a company that qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to a financial year, or that would do so but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group—
@ref s 443A(1) Companies within section 443A (src:5938)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 443A(1) the company is within section 443A` MEANS
    `s 443A(1) the company is described by section 443A` facts

-- s 444(6) in the second text: "This section does not apply to companies within section 443A". The first text has no such
-- sentence, so in the first text no section excludes a company from section 444.
-- src:5993 | (6) This section does not apply to companies within section 443A (filing obligations of companies that qualify as micro-entities).
@ref s 444(6) [text 2] This section does not apply to companies within section 443A (src:5993)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444(6) the company is within a section that excludes it from section 444` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `s 441 the text of the sections the file prints twice that the caller relies on`
    WHEN `s 441 first text in the file` THEN JUST FALSE -- internal: the first text names no excluding section
    WHEN `s 441 second text in the file` THEN `s 443A(1) the company is within section 443A` facts

-- src:5949 | (1) The directors of a company subject to the small companies regime—
-- src:5983 | (1) The directors of a company that is subject to the small companies regime in relation to a financial year, or that would be so subject but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group, must deliver to the registrar a copy of—
@ref s 444(1) Companies within section 444 (src:5949 and src:5983)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444(1) the company is within section 444` MEANS
    `s 441 both are true`
        (`s 444(1) the company is described by section 444` facts)
        (`s 441 the opposite of` (`s 444(6) the company is within a section that excludes it from section 444` facts))

-- src:6004 | (5) This section does not apply to companies within section 444 (filing obligations of companies subject to the small companies regime).
@ref s 444A(5) This section does not apply to companies within section 444 (src:6004)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444A(5) the company is within a section that excludes it from section 444A` MEANS
    `s 444(1) the company is within section 444` facts

-- src:5995 | (1) The directors of a company that is entitled to small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report for a financial year—
@ref s 444A(1) Companies within section 444A (src:5995)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444A(1) the company is within section 444A` MEANS
    `s 441 both are true`
        (`s 444A(1) the company is described by section 444A` facts)
        (`s 441 the opposite of` (`s 444A(5) the company is within a section that excludes it from section 444A` facts))

-- s 445(7): the first text excludes companies within 444 or 444A; the second, companies within 443A or 444.
-- src:6019 | (7) This section does not apply to companies within—
-- src:6020 | (a) section 444 (filing obligations of companies subject to the small companies regime), or
-- src:6021 | (b) section 444A (filing obligations of companies entitled to small companies exemption in relation to directors' report).
-- src:6022 | (7) This section does not apply to companies within—
-- src:6023 | (a) section 443A (filing obligations of micro-entities), or
-- src:6024 | (b) section 444 (filing obligations of small companies other than micro-entities).
@ref s 445(7) This section does not apply to companies within ... (src:6019-6024)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445(7) the company is within a section that excludes it from section 445` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `s 441 the text of the sections the file prints twice that the caller relies on`
    WHEN `s 441 first text in the file` THEN
        `s 441 either is true` (`s 444(1) the company is within section 444` facts) (`s 444A(1) the company is within section 444A` facts)
    WHEN `s 441 second text in the file` THEN
        `s 441 either is true` (`s 443A(1) the company is within section 443A` facts) (`s 444(1) the company is within section 444` facts)

-- src:6006 | (1)) The directors of a company that qualifies as a medium-sized company in relation to a financial year (see sections 465 to 467) must deliver to the registrar a copy of—
@ref s 445(1) Companies within section 445 (src:6006)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445(1) the company is within section 445` MEANS
    `s 441 both are true`
        (`s 445(1) the company is described by section 445` facts)
        (`s 441 the opposite of` (`s 445(7) the company is within a section that excludes it from section 445` facts))

-- s 446(5): the first text excludes companies within 444, 444A or 445; the second, companies within 443A, 444 or 445.
-- src:6039 | (5) This section does not apply to companies within—
-- src:6040 | (a) section 444 (filing obligations of companies subject to the small companies regime), . . .
-- src:6041 | (aa) section 444A (filing obligations of companies entitled to small companies exemption in relation to directors' report), or
-- src:6042 | (b) section 445 (filing obligations of medium-sized companies).
-- src:6043 | (5) This section does not apply to companies within—
-- src:6044 | (a) section 443A (filing obligations of micro-entities),
-- src:6045 | (b) section 444 (filing obligations of small companies other than micro-entities), or
-- src:6046 | (c) section 445 (filing obligations of medium-sized companies).
@ref s 446(5) This section does not apply to companies within ... (src:6039-6046)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 446(5) the company is within a section that excludes it from section 446` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `s 441 the text of the sections the file prints twice that the caller relies on`
    WHEN `s 441 first text in the file` THEN
        `s 441 either is true`
            (`s 441 either is true` (`s 444(1) the company is within section 444` facts) (`s 444A(1) the company is within section 444A` facts))
            (`s 445(1) the company is within section 445` facts)
    WHEN `s 441 second text in the file` THEN
        `s 441 either is true`
            (`s 441 either is true` (`s 443A(1) the company is within section 443A` facts) (`s 444(1) the company is within section 444` facts))
            (`s 445(1) the company is within section 445` facts)

-- src:6026 | (1) The directors of an unquoted company must deliver to the registrar for each financial year of the company a copy of—
@ref s 446(1) Companies within section 446 (src:6026)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 446(1) the company is within section 446` MEANS
    `s 441 both are true`
        (`s 446(1) the company is described by section 446` facts)
        (`s 441 the opposite of` (`s 446(5) the company is within a section that excludes it from section 446` facts))

-- ---- the answer to "does section N apply to this company?", one function per section ----

-- src:5938 | (1) The directors of a company that qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to a financial year, or that would do so but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group—
@ref s 443A(1) Does section 443A apply to the company (src:5938)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 443A(1) section 443A applies to the company` MEANS
    `s 441(1) a filing section applies given its description and its exclusions`
        (`s 443A(1) the company is described by section 443A` facts)
        (JUST FALSE) -- section 443A has no sentence excluding any company

-- src:5949 | (1) The directors of a company subject to the small companies regime—
-- src:5983 | (1) The directors of a company that is subject to the small companies regime in relation to a financial year, or that would be so subject but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group, must deliver to the registrar a copy of—
-- src:5993 | (6) This section does not apply to companies within section 443A (filing obligations of companies that qualify as micro-entities).
@ref s 444(1), (6) Does section 444 apply to the company (src:5949 and src:5983 and src:5993)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444(1) section 444 applies to the company` MEANS
    `s 441(1) a filing section applies given its description and its exclusions`
        (`s 444(1) the company is described by section 444` facts)
        (`s 444(6) the company is within a section that excludes it from section 444` facts)

-- src:5995 | (1) The directors of a company that is entitled to small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report for a financial year—
-- src:6004 | (5) This section does not apply to companies within section 444 (filing obligations of companies subject to the small companies regime).
@ref s 444A(1), (5) Does section 444A apply to the company (src:5995 and src:6004)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444A(1) section 444A applies to the company` MEANS
    `s 441(1) a filing section applies given its description and its exclusions`
        (`s 444A(1) the company is described by section 444A` facts)
        (`s 444A(5) the company is within a section that excludes it from section 444A` facts)

-- src:6006 | (1)) The directors of a company that qualifies as a medium-sized company in relation to a financial year (see sections 465 to 467) must deliver to the registrar a copy of—
-- src:6019 | (7) This section does not apply to companies within—
-- src:6020 | (a) section 444 (filing obligations of companies subject to the small companies regime), or
-- src:6021 | (b) section 444A (filing obligations of companies entitled to small companies exemption in relation to directors' report).
-- src:6022 | (7) This section does not apply to companies within—
-- src:6023 | (a) section 443A (filing obligations of micro-entities), or
-- src:6024 | (b) section 444 (filing obligations of small companies other than micro-entities).
@ref s 445(1), (7) Does section 445 apply to the company (src:6006 and src:6019-6024)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 445(1) section 445 applies to the company` MEANS
    `s 441(1) a filing section applies given its description and its exclusions`
        (`s 445(1) the company is described by section 445` facts)
        (`s 445(7) the company is within a section that excludes it from section 445` facts)

-- src:6026 | (1) The directors of an unquoted company must deliver to the registrar for each financial year of the company a copy of—
-- src:6039 | (5) This section does not apply to companies within—
-- src:6040 | (a) section 444 (filing obligations of companies subject to the small companies regime), . . .
-- src:6041 | (aa) section 444A (filing obligations of companies entitled to small companies exemption in relation to directors' report), or
-- src:6042 | (b) section 445 (filing obligations of medium-sized companies).
-- src:6043 | (5) This section does not apply to companies within—
-- src:6044 | (a) section 443A (filing obligations of micro-entities),
-- src:6045 | (b) section 444 (filing obligations of small companies other than micro-entities), or
-- src:6046 | (c) section 445 (filing obligations of medium-sized companies).
@ref s 446(1), (5) Does section 446 apply to the company (src:6026 and src:6039-6046)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 446(1) section 446 applies to the company` MEANS
    `s 441(1) a filing section applies given its description and its exclusions`
        (`s 446(1) the company is described by section 446` facts)
        (`s 446(5) the company is within a section that excludes it from section 446` facts)

-- src:6048 | (1) The directors of a quoted company must deliver to the registrar for each financial year of the company a copy of—
@ref s 447(1) Does section 447 apply to the company (src:6048)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 447(1) section 447 applies to the company` MEANS
    `s 441(1) a filing section applies given its description and its exclusions`
        (`s 447(1) the company is described by section 447` facts)
        (JUST FALSE) -- section 447 has no sentence excluding any company

-- ---- s 441(1): the section under which the accounts and reports are required ----
-- Exactly one section applies to a company that the text sorts: that one. None applies (no description fits) or several do
-- (in the first text of s 444 a micro-entity is also a company subject to the small companies regime, and neither section
-- excludes the other): the text does not say which governs, so NOTHING.
-- src:5898 | (1) The directors of a company must deliver to the registrar for each financial year the accounts and reports required by—
-- src:5899 | section 443A (filing obligations of micro-entities),
-- src:5900 | section 444 (filing obligations of companies subject to small companies regime small companies other than micro-entities),
-- src:5901 | section 444A (filing obligations of companies entitled to small companies exemption in relation to directors' report),
-- src:5902 | section 445 (filing obligations of medium-sized companies),
-- src:5903 | section 446 (filing obligations of unquoted companies), or
-- src:5904 | section 447 (filing obligations of quoted companies).
@ref s 441(1) The accounts and reports required by section 443A, 444, 444A, 445, 446 or 447 (src:5898-5904)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 441 filing section`
`s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` MEANS
    LET a MEANS `s 443A(1) section 443A applies to the company` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE
        b MEANS `s 444(1) section 444 applies to the company` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE
        c MEANS `s 444A(1) section 444A applies to the company` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE
        d MEANS `s 445(1) section 445 applies to the company` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE
        e MEANS `s 446(1) section 446 applies to the company` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE
        f MEANS `s 447(1) section 447 applies to the company` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE
        howmany MEANS (IF a THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS (IF b THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS (IF c THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS (IF d THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS (IF e THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS (IF f THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    IN IF howmany EQUALS 1
       THEN BRANCH
                IF a THEN JUST `s 441 section 443A`
                IF b THEN JUST `s 441 section 444`
                IF c THEN JUST `s 441 section 444A`
                IF d THEN JUST `s 441 section 445`
                IF e THEN JUST `s 441 section 446`
                OTHERWISE JUST `s 441 section 447`
       ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no description fits the company, or several do and the text does not say which governs

-- ---- s 441(2): the duty is subject to ss 448 and 448A ----
-- src:5905 | (2) This is subject to—
-- src:5906 | section 448 (unlimited companies exempt from filing obligations), and
-- src:5907 | section 448A (dormant subsidiaries exempt from filing obligations).
@ref s 441(2) The duty is subject to the exemptions in ss 448 and 448A (src:5905-5907)
GIVEN `s 448(1) the directors of the unlimited company are not required to deliver accounts and reports` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 448A(1) the directors of the dormant subsidiary are not required to deliver a copy of the individual accounts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 441(2) the directors must deliver the accounts and reports for the financial year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 441 either is true` `s 448(1) the directors of the unlimited company are not required to deliver accounts and reports` `s 448A(1) the directors of the dormant subsidiary are not required to deliver a copy of the individual accounts`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors of an unlimited company are not required to deliver accounts and reports" (s 448(1)); "The directors of a company are not required to deliver a copy of the company's individual accounts" (s 448A(1))
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an exemption answer is not known

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- What each section requires of the directors, document by document
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Each table answers, for one document, "must", "may" or (where the text says so) "does not require"; a document the
-- section does not mention is NOTHING (silent). "exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption"
-- is a plain fact of the delivery (Part 16's seam).

-- src:5938 | (1) The directors of a company that qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to a financial year, or that would do so but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group—
-- src:5939 | (a) must deliver to the registrar a copy of the company’s annual accounts, and
-- src:5940 | (b) may also deliver to the registrar a copy of the directors’ report.
-- src:5941 | (2) The directors must also deliver to the registrar a copy of the auditor’s report on those accounts (and any directors’ report).
