-- s 441(1) with the section that applies: what the directors must or may deliver, for a company whose classification is given.
-- src:5898 | (1) The directors of a company must deliver to the registrar for each financial year the accounts and reports required by—
-- src:5899 | section 443A (filing obligations of micro-entities),
-- src:5900 | section 444 (filing obligations of companies subject to small companies regime small companies other than micro-entities),
-- src:5901 | section 444A (filing obligations of companies entitled to small companies exemption in relation to directors' report),
-- src:5902 | section 445 (filing obligations of medium-sized companies),
-- src:5903 | section 446 (filing obligations of unquoted companies), or
-- src:5904 | section 447 (filing obligations of quoted companies).
@ref s 441(1) What the section that applies to the company requires of the directors for the document (src:5898-5904)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 441 facts about the company`
      document IS A `s 441 document`
      delivery IS A `s 441 facts about what is delivered`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 441 requirement`
`s 441(1) what the filing section that applies requires of the directors for the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 441(1) the filing section that applies to the company` facts
    WHEN JUST `s 441 section 443A` THEN `s 443A(1) what section 443A requires of the directors for the document` document delivery
    WHEN JUST `s 441 section 444` THEN `s 444(1) what section 444 requires of the directors for the document` (facts's `s 441 the text of the sections the file prints twice that the caller relies on`) document delivery
    WHEN JUST `s 441 section 444A` THEN `s 444A(1) what section 444A requires of the directors for the document` document delivery
    WHEN JUST `s 441 section 445` THEN `s 445(1) what section 445 requires of the directors for the document` document delivery
    WHEN JUST `s 441 section 446` THEN `s 446(1) what section 446 requires of the directors for the document` document delivery
    WHEN JUST `s 441 section 447` THEN `s 447(1) what section 447 requires of the directors for the document` document delivery
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say which of the six sections governs this company

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The copy delivered must state who signed it, and who audited (the same sentences in each section)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 443A(3): the copies of the balance sheet and any directors' report must state the name of the person who signed it on
-- behalf of the board. The same sentence recurs in ss 444(6), 444A(3), 445(5), 446(3) and 447(3) over different documents,
-- so one function takes the documents the section names and the later sections call it.
-- src:5943 | (3) The copies of the balance sheet and any directors’ report delivered to the registrar under this section must state the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board.
@ref s 443A(3) The copies must state the name of the person who signed on behalf of the board (src:5943)
GIVEN `the documents the section names` IS A LIST OF `s 441 document`
      document IS A `s 441 document`
      `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 443A(3) the copy of a document the section names meets the requirement to state who signed it` MEANS
    IF elem document `the documents the section names`
    THEN IF `the copy states the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must state the name of the person who signed it on behalf of the board"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section names only certain documents

