-- s 443A(4) and (5): the copy of the auditor's report must state the name of the auditor (and, for a firm, of the person who
-- signed as senior statutory auditor), or, if the s 506 conditions are met, that a resolution has been passed and notified.
-- The s 506 answer is another part's (coa12) and is an INPUT of type MAYBE BOOLEAN.
DECLARE `s 443A facts about the copy of the auditor's report` HAS
    `s 443A more than one person is appointed as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 443A the copy states the name of the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 443A the copy states the names of all the auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 443A the auditor is a firm` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 443A the copy states the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 506 the conditions in section 506 for omitting the names are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 443A the copy states that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State in accordance with section 506` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:5947 | (5) If more than one person is appointed as auditor, the reference in subsection (4)(a) to the name of the auditor is to be read as a reference to the names of all the auditors.
@ref s 443A(5) More than one auditor: the names of all the auditors (src:5947)
GIVEN `more than one person is appointed as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 443A(5) the reference to the name of the auditor is a reference to the names of all the auditors` MEANS
    IF `more than one person is appointed as auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "If" not met): "If more than one person is appointed as auditor, the reference ... is to be read as a reference to the names of all the auditors"

-- src:5944 | (4) The copy of the auditor’s report delivered to the registrar under this section must—
-- src:5945 | (a) state the name of the auditor and (where the auditor is a firm) the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor, or
-- src:5946 | (b) if the conditions in section 506 (circumstances in which names may be omitted) are met, state that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State in accordance with that section.
@ref s 443A(4) The copy of the auditor's report must state the name of the auditor, or the s 506 resolution (src:5944-5946)
GIVEN copy IS A `s 443A facts about the copy of the auditor's report`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 443A(4) the copy of the auditor's report states what the section requires` MEANS
    LET `the names the section requires are stated` MEANS
            IF `s 443A(5) the reference to the name of the auditor is a reference to the names of all the auditors` (copy's `s 443A more than one person is appointed as auditor`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN copy's `s 443A the copy states the names of all the auditors`
            ELSE copy's `s 443A the copy states the name of the auditor`
        `limb (a) is met` MEANS
                `the names the section requires are stated`
            AND (   (NOT (copy's `s 443A the auditor is a firm`))
                 OR copy's `s 443A the copy states the name of the person who signed it as senior statutory auditor`)
        `limb (b) is met` MEANS
            `s 441 both are true`
                (copy's `s 506 the conditions in section 506 for omitting the names are met`)
                (JUST (copy's `s 443A the copy states that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State in accordance with section 506`))
    IN IF `limb (a) is met`
       THEN JUST TRUE
       ELSE CONSIDER `limb (b) is met`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The copy of the auditor's report delivered to the registrar under this section must— (a) state the name of the auditor ... or (b) if the conditions in section 506 ... are met, state that a resolution has been passed"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section 506 conditions are met is not known

