-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 444 (first text): the statements a small company's balance sheet must carry when it files less
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5961 | (5) Where the directors of a company subject to the small companies regime ...—
-- src:5962 | (a) do not deliver to the registrar a copy of the company's profit and loss account, or
-- src:5963 | (b) do not deliver to the registrar a copy of the directors' report,
-- src:5964 | the copy of the balance sheet delivered to the registrar must contain in a prominent position a statement that the company's annual accounts and reports have been delivered in accordance with the provisions applicable to companies subject to the small companies regime.
@ref s 444(5) Where the profit and loss account or the directors' report is not delivered, the balance sheet must carry a statement (src:5961-5964)
GIVEN `the directors do not deliver a copy of the profit and loss account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors do not deliver a copy of the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444(5) the section requires the copy of the balance sheet to contain the statement` MEANS
    IF `the directors do not deliver a copy of the profit and loss account` OR `the directors do not deliver a copy of the directors' report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "where" not met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "Where the directors of a company subject to the small companies regime ... (a) do not deliver ... a copy of the company's profit and loss account, or (b) do not deliver ... a copy of the directors' report"

-- src:5961 | (5) Where the directors of a company subject to the small companies regime ...—
-- src:5962 | (a) do not deliver to the registrar a copy of the company's profit and loss account, or
-- src:5963 | (b) do not deliver to the registrar a copy of the directors' report,
-- src:5964 | the copy of the balance sheet delivered to the registrar must contain in a prominent position a statement that the company's annual accounts and reports have been delivered in accordance with the provisions applicable to companies subject to the small companies regime.
@ref s 444(5) The copy of the balance sheet must contain in a prominent position the statement (src:5961-5964)
GIVEN `the directors do not deliver a copy of the profit and loss account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors do not deliver a copy of the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy contains in a prominent position a statement that the company's annual accounts and reports have been delivered in accordance with the provisions applicable to companies subject to the small companies regime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444(5) the copy of the balance sheet contains the statement the section requires` MEANS
    IF `s 444(5) the section requires the copy of the balance sheet to contain the statement` `the directors do not deliver a copy of the profit and loss account` `the directors do not deliver a copy of the directors' report` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the copy contains in a prominent position a statement that the company's annual accounts and reports have been delivered in accordance with the provisions applicable to companies subject to the small companies regime`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the copy of the balance sheet delivered to the registrar must contain in a prominent position a statement"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the statement is required only where the profit and loss account or the directors' report is not delivered

-- (5C) first: it decides whether (5A) applies at all.
-- src:5965 | (5A) Subject to subsection (5C), where the directors of a company subject to the small companies regime do not deliver to the registrar a copy of the company’s profit and loss account—
-- src:5975 | (5C) Subsection (5A) does not apply in relation to a company if—
-- src:5976 | (a) the company qualifies as a micro-entity (see sections 384A and 384B) in relation to a financial year, and
-- src:5977 | (b) the company’s accounts are prepared for that year in accordance with any of the micro-entity provisions.
@ref s 444(5A), (5C) Subsection (5A) does not apply to a micro-entity whose accounts follow the micro-entity provisions (src:5965 and src:5975-5977)
GIVEN `the directors do not deliver a copy of the profit and loss account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 384A the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company's accounts are prepared for that year in accordance with any of the micro-entity provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444(5C) subsection (5A) applies to the company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the directors do not deliver a copy of the profit and loss account`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "where" not met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "where the directors of a company subject to the small companies regime do not deliver to the registrar a copy of the company's profit and loss account"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 441 both are true` `s 384A the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year` (JUST `the company's accounts are prepared for that year in accordance with any of the micro-entity provisions`)
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (5A) does not apply in relation to a company if— (a) the company qualifies as a micro-entity ... and (b) the company's accounts are prepared for that year in accordance with any of the micro-entity provisions."
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company qualifies as a micro-entity is not known

-- src:5965 | (5A) Subject to subsection (5C), where the directors of a company subject to the small companies regime do not deliver to the registrar a copy of the company’s profit and loss account—
-- src:5966 | (a) the copy of the balance sheet delivered to the registrar must disclose that fact, and
@ref s 444(5A)(a) The copy of the balance sheet must disclose that the profit and loss account is not delivered (src:5965-5966)
GIVEN `subsection (5A) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444(5A)(a) the section requires the copy of the balance sheet to disclose that the profit and loss account is not delivered` MEANS
    `subsection (5A) applies`

-- src:5965 | (5A) Subject to subsection (5C), where the directors of a company subject to the small companies regime do not deliver to the registrar a copy of the company’s profit and loss account—
-- src:5967 | (b) unless the company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption, the notes to the balance sheet delivered must satisfy the requirements in subsection (5B).
@ref s 444(5A)(b) Unless exempt from audit, the notes to the balance sheet must satisfy subsection (5B) (src:5965 and src:5967)
GIVEN `subsection (5A) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444(5A)(b) the section requires the notes to the balance sheet to satisfy the requirements in subsection (5B)` MEANS
    IF `the company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "unless" met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "unless the company is exempt from audit and the directors have taken advantage of that exemption"
    ELSE `subsection (5A) applies`

-- src:5968 | (5B) Those requirements are that the notes to the balance sheet must—
-- src:5969 | (a) state whether the auditor’s report was qualified or unqualified,
-- src:5970 | (b) where that report was qualified, disclose the basis of the qualification (reproducing any statement under section 498(2)(a) or (b) or section 498(3), if applicable),
-- src:5971 | (c) where that report was unqualified, include a reference to any matters to which the auditor drew attention by way of emphasis, and
-- src:5972 | (d) state—
-- src:5973 | (i) the name of the auditor and (where the auditor is a firm) the name of the person who signed the auditor’s report as senior statutory auditor, or
-- src:5974 | (ii) if the conditions in section 506 (circumstances in which names may be omitted) are met, that a resolution has been passed and notified to the Secretary of State in accordance with that section.
@ref s 444(5B) The requirements for the notes to the balance sheet (src:5968-5974)
GIVEN `the auditor's report was qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notes state whether the auditor's report was qualified or unqualified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notes disclose the basis of the qualification, reproducing any statement under section 498(2)(a) or (b) or section 498(3), if applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notes include a reference to any matters to which the auditor drew attention by way of emphasis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notes state the auditor as paragraph (d) requires` IS A `s 443A facts about the copy of the auditor's report`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 444(5B) the notes to the balance sheet satisfy the requirements` MEANS
    LET `paragraphs (a) to (c) are met` MEANS
                `the notes state whether the auditor's report was qualified or unqualified`
            AND (IF `the auditor's report was qualified`
                 THEN `the notes disclose the basis of the qualification, reproducing any statement under section 498(2)(a) or (b) or section 498(3), if applicable`
                 ELSE `the notes include a reference to any matters to which the auditor drew attention by way of emphasis`)
    IN IF NOT `paragraphs (a) to (c) are met`
       THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Those requirements are that the notes to the balance sheet must— (a) state whether the auditor's report was qualified or unqualified, (b) where that report was qualified, disclose the basis of the qualification ... (c) where that report was unqualified, include a reference to any matters to which the auditor drew attention by way of emphasis"
       ELSE `s 441 both are true` (JUST TRUE) (`s 443A(4) the copy of the auditor's report states what the section requires` `the notes state the auditor as paragraph (d) requires`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 441: the directors' duty as a regulative rule (the deadline is s 442's period for filing, counted in days from the
-- end of the accounting reference period; the consequence is the offence in s 451(1))
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5898 | (1) The directors of a company must deliver to the registrar for each financial year the accounts and reports required by—
-- src:5909 | (1) This section specifies the period allowed for the directors of a company to comply with their obligation under section 441 to deliver accounts and reports for a financial year to the registrar.
@ref s 441(1) The directors must deliver the accounts and reports within the period for filing (src:5898 and src:5909)
GIVEN `the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the end of the period for filing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 441(1) the directors' duty to deliver the accounts and reports` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Director, Registrar, "deliver to the registrar the accounts and reports required by section 443A, 444, 444A, 445, 446 or 447"
    WITHIN `the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the end of the period for filing` -- days, counted from the end of the accounting reference period (s 442)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "s 451(1): the requirements of section 441 were not complied with before the end of the period for filing"

-- The same duty as a decision function over the facts (a DEONTIC value cannot be compared in an #ASSERT, and a #TRACE moves
-- no assertion count): were the requirements complied with before the end of the period for filing? The day is counted from
-- the end of the accounting reference period; delivered on the last day of the period is delivered before it ends
-- ("the period ends with" that date, s 443(2)). Not delivered at all, and the period over: not complied with.
-- src:5898 | (1) The directors of a company must deliver to the registrar for each financial year the accounts and reports required by—
-- src:5909 | (1) This section specifies the period allowed for the directors of a company to comply with their obligation under section 441 to deliver accounts and reports for a financial year to the registrar.
@ref s 441(1) Were the requirements complied with before the end of the period for filing (src:5898 and src:5909)
GIVEN `the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the end of the period for filing` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the day the accounts and reports were delivered (if they have been)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the period for filing has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 441(1) the requirements were complied with before the end of the period for filing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the day the accounts and reports were delivered (if they have been)`
    WHEN JUST delivered THEN
        IF delivered AT MOST `the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the end of the period for filing`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling of 2026-11-05): "before the end of the period for filing"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the period for filing has ended`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling of 2026-11-05): "are not complied with ... before the end of the period for filing"
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the period has not ended and nothing has been delivered yet
